"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — and none of them means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything without ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domains or "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument ["},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes for "},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". # Every bound here is a security control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written by hand cannot lift them."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/RefreshReuseResponse":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RefreshReuseResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RefreshReuseResponse","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshReuseResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RefreshReuseResponse","abstract":[{"text":"What the token endpoint does when a refresh token that has already been rotated is presented","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"refused","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (G-C, #818 — the T-254 amendment). Two values, ordered by strictness:","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/refreshreuseresponse","role":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}